{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Decode\/timeout(_:customError:)"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timeout","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuspendingClock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"duration"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"customError"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws before the first element."}]},{"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading","level":2},{"code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeoutError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"customError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") when ","type":"text"},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" passes between elements, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any error the upstream throws.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Throws","type":"aside"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"text":") holds the one thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"timeout(_:customError:)","modules":[{"relatedModules":["_Concurrency"],"name":"Afluent"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"customError"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":")?) -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","text":"AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","text":"Timeout","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV","text":"SuspendingClock","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"TimeoutSequence.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/TimeoutSequence.swift#L176"},"platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"deprecated":false,"unavail